-- g7-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT to fail.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Each assertion states the answer of a reading that the fork register in FRAGMENT-G7.md
-- considered and did NOT take, against the function that takes the other reading.  So each must fail while the encoding
-- stands.  The file is counted: check-g7.sh lists its count of failed assertions as expected, and the final report
-- states it.  It doubles as proof that the harness can fail: an assertion that could not fail would be no test.
-- An assertion is placed here only if the reading taken gives an ANSWER; where the reading taken refuses (for
-- example Chapter 6 with no section 46 regulation), a plain assertion would be "refused", which is not a failure, so
-- those forks are tested green in g7-tests-commencement.l4 with their alternative function instead.

§ `Assertions that fail by design`

GIVEN pub IS A DATE
      regs59 IS A DATE
      regs46 IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts: published on` pub `, section 59 regulations in force on` regs59 `, section 46 regulations in force on` regs46 MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS pub
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS regs59
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS regs46

GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts as the sources give them` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2027 1 16

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with 14 and 15 April 2025 as days of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2025 4 14, YMD 2025 4 15

GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with propane only` MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 12, `refrigerants` IS LIST (Refrigerant OF "290", TRUE)

GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with unlawful propane only` MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 12, `refrigerants` IS LIST (Refrigerant OF "290", FALSE)

GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with propane and R134a` MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 12, `refrigerants` IS LIST (Refrigerant OF "290", TRUE), (Refrigerant OF "134a", TRUE)

GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`work on` system `on` day MEANS
    `the Law has commenced for work on the system` system `on the day` day `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them`

§§ `F-C-3: three months counted from the later of the two days`

#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16

§§ `F-C-1 and F-C-4: IL s.10(c) applied; the Law commencing on the day after the period ends`

-- 16.1.2027 is a Saturday; both rejected readings end on Sunday 17.1.2027.
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- With 14 and 15 April 2025 as rest days the first limb moves to 16.4.2025 on that reading; the reading taken keeps 14.4.2025.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 16

§§ `F-C-2: its publication taken as the day the Knesset passed the Law`

#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 8

§§ `F-C-5: the whole of the commencement day is not yet bound (the one-minute gap of IL s.21 read at day level)`

#ASSERT NOT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16)

§§ `F-C-6a and F-C-6b: a mixed system governed by the later paragraph; a listed refrigerant of unlawful use governed by paragraph (1)`

#ASSERT NOT `work on` `a system with propane and R134a` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with unlawful propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16)

§§ `T19: Chapter 6 commences on the first limb alone, with section 46 regulations that come later ignored`

#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

§§ `T7: the three years of the Second Schedule counted from paragraph (2)'s date and not from the commencement day`

#ASSERT `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (`the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts as the sources give them`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 16

§§ `F-S4-1: item (66) as the wiki has it, 170E, and the tolerant reading of designations`

#ASSERT `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "170E"
#ASSERT NOT `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "E170"
#ASSERT `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "600A"
#ASSERT `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "R290"
#ASSERT `the designation is printed in the Fourth Schedule` "1234YF"

§§ `F-E-1: section 58 and section 61 opening the same electrical work (trap T32)`

-- Electrical work on a cooling system that the First Schedule does not list: the two readings do not agree.
#ASSERT `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 58 as a wide gateway` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) TRUE EQUALS `electrical work is open to the licensee, reading section 61 as the only gateway` (LIST `grade 1 licence`) TRUE FALSE

§§ `F-A-1 (courts): section 62 additional to section 56, against section 56 as the only route (trap T39)`

#ASSERT `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 62 as additional to section 56` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the fora for review of a decision, reading section 56 as the only route for a final decision of the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE

§§ `F-R-1: five heads of fee, as the survey counted them`

#ASSERT count `s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee` EQUALS 5

§§ `F-R-2: paragraph (1) read as covering the matters of paragraph (2), so that approval is required for the manner of applying for a licence`

GIVETH A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
`neither approval nor consultation` MEANS
    `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` WITH
        `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS FALSE
        `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew` `has been followed, given the procedure` `neither approval nor consultation`

§§ `F-R-6: the last day for an application to renew, with IL s.10(c) not applied to a nominal last day that falls on a day of rest`

GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2026 3 21

#ASSERT `s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 21)) `the calendar with Saturday 21 March 2026 as a day of rest` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 21
